# What not to send to the Docker daemon as build context.
#
# The distribution images in containers/ do COPY . /src, so everything here is
# copied into every one of them unless it is excluded.  The repository is around
# 270 MB, of which 105 MB is .git and most of the rest is documentation PDFs and
# whatever a local build has left behind; none of that is needed to build and
# test PSOPT, and all of it is transferred once per image.
#
# Nothing in containers/common/build_and_test.sh reads the git history, so
# excluding .git is safe.  If a future step wants the version from git, it will
# have to be passed in as a build argument instead.

.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore

# Local build trees.  Copying one in would not break the build, since the
# container configures into its own directory, but it is the largest avoidable
# part of the context and a stale CMakeCache.txt inside it names paths that do
# not exist in the image.
build/
build-*/
*/build/

# Editor and operating system detritus.
*~
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# Documentation is built and published elsewhere; the PDFs are large and no
# test reads them.
doc/*.pdf
*.pdf
